      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2024-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Pull out the common power: \\(7^{2024} + 7^{2025} + 7^{2026}\\) \\(= 7^{2024}(1 + 7 + 49)\\) \\(= 7^{2024} \\cdot 57.\\) And \\(57 = 3 \\cdot 19,\\) so the product is a multiple of \\(19.\\) The remainder is \\(0.\\) Thus, A is the correct answer.",
